# .ignore — ripgrep-only re-admission (NOT a git ignore file)
#
# This is not `.gitignore` and git never reads it. It exists because ripgrep
# applies `.ignore` *before* `.gitignore`, so `!graft/` here overrides the
# `/graft/` rule in .gitignore and makes the graft graph searchable while it
# stays untracked.
#
# Why that matters: `graft/` holds the repo context graph (INDEX.md + one card
# per file, ~1290 files) that `graft ask` / `graft grep` and the AGENTS.md
# workflow depend on. Verified: removing this file drops graft/ from ripgrep's
# file list from 1290 files to 0.
#
# `.cache/` and `.graph/` stay excluded — they are the index/cache internals,
# not documentation.
#
# See AGENTS.md §Graft and docs/PROJECT_STATUS.md.

# graft's cards are gitignored but should stay greppable.
!graft/
graft/.cache/
graft/.graph/
